Z||000003||Seanh||10-12-2000||07:36 AM||||Im my setup, I have one 10" up front and ported into the pass. side floor. I also put 12" behind the seats for SPL comp. Check out this site: <A HREF="http://www.perigee.net/%7elunapark/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.perigee.net/%7elunapark/</A>   he put a box like mine up front, but with 2 10's instead of one. You would have to put some work into it, but it can be done, you also have to loose your spare tire and jack. The box is stereo, meaning the subs space is kept seperate, and its 4th order bandpass design.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000004||goldfinger||10-12-2000||02:19 PM||||My system is as follows:<BR>HU: Pioneer Premier 920<BR>Speakers:<BR>Dash: Infinty Kappa 5 1/4 Comp set<BR>Doors: Infinty Perfect 6.1 comp set<BR>Sides: Infinty Kappa 4 x 6 plates<BR>Subs: 2 12" Infinty Perfect<BR>Amps:<BR>Subs: JBL 1200.1 <BR>Doors: JBL P180.2<BR>Sides & Dash: P80.4<P>This system should slam, it has all the necessarys like highs, mids, lows. It should play very high and sound crystal clear. I am going to put one 12" in the back of the car and one 12" perfect in the spare tire compartment with pips to get the bass inside the cab.I will take pictures of me making all this.<BR><P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
